uted to its original authors. It mentions Wen Li holds 40 lines of potential inheritance, but nothing on the mechanical-change point.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A gives a bus factor of 3, which is an explicit fail condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A says 79% of lines belong to inactive people, and Felix's 43.5% would have no author left. It never gives the ~85% combined figure. Its numbers are inconsistent and do not match the 38% departed plus Felix's share.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A does not clearly name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann and mochalins as having left. It lists the active ones as Dhole, Wen Li and Krzysztof Wolicki. It also says Felix is inactive within 365 days, which is wrong. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B puts Felix at 36% of all lines including the generated table, and 46% without it. Its headline figure is 36%, below 40%, though the 46% excluding the table is stated. Since the table is generated and excluded in the truth, the 46% is close to the 47.2%, but the table shows 36%. This is borderline. The answer names Felix top and gives 46% for the hand-written code, which is within 43-52%.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B gives Wen Li 4% without the table, above 2.5%. It also names Tobias Ek as a recent committer with 2 lines. It does not say help.zig stays with its original authors by percentage. It treats the width table as possibly not generated.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B gives a bus factor of 2, but via Felix plus Wen Li, not jnagpaul. It does not say jnagpaul stopped contributing in 2023 as the second person. Actually it does mention jnagpaul last commit 2023 under gone quiet. But the bus factor of 2 rests on a Wen Li table-inflated figure. Felix's 46% is stated as just under half, but the answer does not say he needs a second person from the clean set. This is borderline, and the 36% headline means it falls short.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B gives 36-46% as the loss if Felix left and separately 37% for people with no recent commits. It never combines them into about 85%. It frames the loss as Felix's own share only.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B names jnagpaul (2023), Vincent Rischmann (2025) and mochalins (2025) as gone quiet. It says Felix is still active. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion, and it treats Dmitri's date as a clock oddity.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C reports Felix at 37% with the table, and about 48% without it. Its headline figure is 37%, but the 48% for hand-written code is within 43-52%.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C says Wen Li's remaining 68 lines are small, which is about 3%, above 2.5%. It says Felix wrote only 1 of help.zig's lines. It does not say help.zig remains attributed to jnagpaul at about 49% and Dhole at 23%. It does not address Tobias Ek's share.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives a bus factor of about 2 using Felix and Wen. It does not use jnagpaul or say he stopped contributing in 2023, and it says Felix is near 50% alone only without the table.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives only Felix's 37% as the loss and does not add the share owned by people who already left.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as having left. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"D\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer D merges Felix's three names and gets about 39% of lines, below 40%. It names Felix top, but the figure is outside 43-52%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer D says help.zig is 100% Tobias Ek. That is a fail condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer D gives a bus factor of about 4. That is 3 or more, a fail condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer D gives only Felix's 39%. It says 9 of 13 files are mostly inactive, but gives no combined figure of about 85%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer D counts Felix as inactive with no commit in 6 months, which marks him as having left. It credits help.zig to Tobias Ek.\", \"pass\": false}], \"E\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer E merges four emails and gets 37% with the table. It does not give a no-table figure for Felix, so the share is outside 43-52%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer E gives Wen Li 25% and calls Tobias Ek's owner listing wrong. It treats the table as only possibly generated. It does not say help.zig stays with jnagpaul and Dhole in percentage terms.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer E gives a bus factor of about 2 for the repo but does not name jnagpaul or say he stopped in 2023. It says Felix at 37% has no majority.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer E gives only Felix's 37% as the loss and says no part of the code is fully orphaned. It does not mention the already departed authors.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer E does not name jnagpaul, Vincent Rischmann or mochalins as having left. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"F\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer F merges Felix and gets 35.8% with the generated table included. That is below 40%, and it does not give a no-table figure.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer F gives Wen Li 26%, counting the width table as code someone wrote. This fails the generated-table condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer F gives a bus factor of 2 via Felix plus Wen Li at 61.8%, not jnagpaul. It lists jnagpaul as not active but does not say he stopped in 2023. It says Felix is at 35.8%, which is below half.\", \"